{
  "title": "What Happens When Code Runs?",
  "subtitle": "The Top-to-Bottom Order of Execution",
  "topic": "1.3 • RUNNING YOUR CODE",
  "body": "<div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; width: 100%;\"><div style=\"text-align: center; margin-bottom: 8px; width: 100%;\"><div style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 4px 4px 0px #111111; padding: 4px 14px; margin-bottom: 12px; font-weight: 900; font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px;\">1.3 • Program Flow & Execution</div><h1 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 32px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 8px 0; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: -0.5px;\">The Order of <hlt>Execution</hlt></h1><p style=\"font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; color: #222222; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 600px;\">When you press Run, how does the computer actually execute your code? Let's trace it step-by-step.</p></div><div style=\"background: #fef08a; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 22px; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">1. Top-to-Bottom Flow</span><h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">Like Reading a Recipe</h2><p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">Python reads code just like a human reads a book: <strong>from top to bottom, one line at a time</strong>. It never jumps ahead or skips lines on its own. Each <hlt>print()</hlt> statement outputs on its own new line in the console (e.g. <hlt>print(10)</hlt> then <hlt>print(20)</hlt> prints 10 and 20 on separate lines).</p><div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;\"><div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px 14px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;\"><span style=\"font-family: monospace; font-weight: bold; color: #0284c7;\">Line 1: print(\"First\")</span><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; background: #e0f2fe; border: 1px solid #111111; padding: 2px 8px;\">[1] Runs First</span></div><div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px 14px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;\"><span style=\"font-family: monospace; font-weight: bold; color: #16a34a;\">Line 2: print(\"Second\")</span><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; background: #dcfce7; border: 1px solid #111111; padding: 2px 8px;\">[2] Runs Second</span></div><div style=\"background: #ffffff; border: 2px solid #111111; padding: 10px 14px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;\"><span style=\"font-family: monospace; font-weight: bold; color: #d97706;\">Line 3: print(\"Third\")</span><span style=\"font-size: 12px; font-weight: 800; background: #fef3c7; border: 1px solid #111111; padding: 2px 8px;\">[3] Runs Last</span></div></div></div><div style=\"background: #93c5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 22px; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">2. Order Determines Results</span><h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">Sequence is Everything</h2><p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 12px 0; line-height: 1.5;\">If you swap the order of lines in your script, the order of the printed output changes immediately. The computer follows your exact sequence, not what is 'most important'.</p><div style=\"background: #0d1117; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #111111; padding: 12px 16px; font-family: 'Consolas', monospace; color: #f0f6fc; font-size: 14px; border-radius: 4px;\"><span style=\"color: #f472b6;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Game Over\"</span>)<br/><span style=\"color: #f472b6;\">print</span>(<span style=\"color: #a5d6ff;\">\"Welcome Player 1\"</span>)<br/><span style=\"color: #8b949e;\"># Result will output 'Game Over' first because it is written on Line 1!</span></div></div><div style=\"background: #fca5a5; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 22px; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span style=\"display: inline-block; background-color: #ffffff; color: #111111; border: 2px solid #111111; box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px #111111; padding: 2px 8px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 900; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;\">3. What Happens on an Error?</span><h2 style=\"font-family: 'Title', 'Body', sans-serif; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0 0 10px 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">Immediate Halt</h2><p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: #111111; margin: 0; line-height: 1.5;\">If an error occurs on Line 2, all lines <em>before</em> Line 2 execute successfully. But Python immediately halts at Line 2, and lines below it never run.</p></div><div style=\"background-color: #c4b5fd; border: 3px solid #111111; box-shadow: 6px 6px 0px #111111; border-radius: 4px; padding: 16px 20px; text-align: center;\"><p style=\"font-size: 15px; font-weight: 900; color: #111111; margin: 0; text-transform: uppercase;\">Key Rule: Python programs are <hlt>strictly sequential</hlt>—Line 1 finishes before Line 2 starts!</p></div></div>"
}
